Let inotifyd watch a directory through a symbolic link or junction.
The directory check used lstat(), so a link to a directory was rejected
as "not a directory" unless its name ended in a slash, although
CreateFile() follows the link and the watch works. Follow links in the
check too.

---
 miscutils/inotifyd.c |    2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/miscutils/inotifyd.c
+++ b/miscutils/inotifyd.c
@@ -369,7 +369,7 @@
 		if (mask == 0)
 			bb_error_msg_and_die("%s: invalid mask", *argv);
 
-		if (!is_directory(*argv, FALSE))
+		if (!is_directory(*argv, TRUE))
 			bb_error_msg_and_die("%s: not a directory", *argv);
 
 		watch[n].hdir = CreateFile(*argv, GENERIC_READ|FILE_LIST_DIRECTORY,
